    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d311-a1">

                <pb facs="0631" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg507"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[lnclosure 1 in No. 138.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Lord Granville.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation</hi>, &amp;c., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1881-02-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 22,
                    1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    copies of the affidavits<anchor n="*" xml:id="d311-f1"/> of the masters <pb
                        facs="0632" n="508" xml:id="pg508"/> of two United States fishing vessels
                    detailing the acts of violence by which they have been prevented fram exercising
                    their rights of fishing in certain Newfoundland waters, and which are mentioned
                    in the instruction from Mr. Evarts which I had the honor of communicating to
                    your lordship yesterday.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
